<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     THE ORDER TESTS.

     This project exists because of a sentence that was true in two places
     and false in the code. docs/CONNECT_API.md promised that
     `range=upcoming` "includes active meetings first", and the comment
     directly above the filter in ListMeetingsAsync said "Live meetings
     first, then what is coming". The query underneath ordered by
     `ScheduledStart ?? CreatedAt` and nothing else, so a scheduled meeting
     nobody ever joined — due an hour ago, still inside the two-hour grace
     window — sorted ABOVE a meeting that was live at that moment.

     Nothing failed. No log line, no error, no 500. The phone's Meetings
     screen simply put the dead meeting at the top and the live one below
     it, and the only way to notice was to be in a meeting and look.

     It survived because the rule could not be RUN. Reading it is what
     everybody did, and reading it is what missed it.

     THREE DELIBERATE CHOICES, the first two copied from tests/connect-wire:

     1. ConnectMeetingOrder.cs and ConnectEntities.cs are LINKED, not
        copied. This compiles the exact files that run in production. A
        copy would drift and the tests would go on passing against code
        nobody ships.

     2. No test framework. A console app with an exit code needs no package
        restore, so it runs on a box with no network, in CI, and on a
        laptop, identically. `dotnet run` and read the last line.

     3. The rule is driven as LINQ-to-objects over a plain List. That
        proves the ORDER — which is the thing that was wrong. It does not
        prove that Npgsql translates the expression to SQL; the API build
        and a real request do that, and the PR that added this file says so
        rather than leaving it to be assumed.

     It is not in any solution file on purpose: nothing about the API build
     should depend on it, and it must never end up published.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>TatvaOS.Tests.Order</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>connect-order-test</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsPublishable>false</IsPublishable>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>false</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The production files themselves. Not copies. -->
    <Compile Include="../../apps/api/Modules/Connect/ConnectMeetingOrder.cs"
             Link="ConnectMeetingOrder.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../apps/api/Modules/Connect/ConnectEntities.cs"
             Link="ConnectEntities.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
